# NFL photo jersey backs (always)

**One silhouette.** Bulky NFL yoke cut with shoulder nameplate, short sleeves with stripe bands, side helmet in frame. Solid `#000` (LED energy). No hanger on photo backs.

**Scale lock:** PNG jersey must fill the frame like the ScammerVille / 49ers reference — **never shrink the jersey** to add collar margin or lift the helmet. CSS uses **width-based** `background-size: 88% auto` (not `auto XX%` height-fit). Overlay positions are tuned per format; the photo scale stays fixed.

**Wordmark:** baked into the PNG only (club on yoke plate). Upright block caps. CSS hides `.soccer-jersey-team` on photo kits.

**Collar:** visible gold collar band in the PNG. If the LED crops the top, nudge `background-position` (e.g. `center 38%`) — **do not** shrink `background-size`.

**Helmet:** kit-secondary helmet on the **right**, overlapping the hem. Regenerate from the current PNG with **identical jersey scale**; only move the helmet upward so the facemask is fully visible.

**Patron name (CSS):** `#displayMain.soccer-jersey-name` — midway yoke ↔ number. `top` ~18% (64×32 ~16%); `height` ~9%; cap ~11.5vh.

**Number (CSS):** `#displaySub.soccer-jersey-number` — `top` ~40% (64×32 ~38%); `height` ~28%; `align-content: center`; cap ~48vh.

**Background (`display.css`):** `background-size: 88% auto`; `background-position: center 38%`.

## GenerateImage prompt (helmet / collar only — same scale)

```
CRITICAL: Keep the reference image EXACTLY — same jersey scale, position, size, camera, silhouette. Do NOT shrink the jersey. Do NOT add margins that make the jersey smaller. ONLY: (1) crisp visible gold collar at neckline if needed; (2) move the side helmet UP so facemask is fully visible. Solid #000000. Print ONLY "{CLUB}" on yoke. No patron name/number. No hanger.
```

